### Auth Service HTTP Tests
### Base URL for local development
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8081
@contentType = application/json

### ===== AUTHENTICATION ENDPOINTS =====

### 1. Register a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@northbridge.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!",
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe"
}

### 2. Register another user for testing
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "jane.smith@northbridge.com",
  "password": "SecurePass456!",
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Smith"
}

### 3. Register with invalid email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "password": "SecurePass123!",
  "firstName": "John",
  "lastName": "Doe"
}

### 4. Register with short password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "test@northbridge.com",
  "password": "123",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User"
}

### 5. Login with valid credentials
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@northbridge.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

### Save token for next requests
@token = token_from_above_response

### 6. Login with invalid password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@northbridge.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword"
}

### 7. Login with non-existent user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "nonexistent@northbridge.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123!"
}

### 8. Get current user profile (requires JWT token from login response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJqb2huLmRvZUBub3J0aGJyaWRnZS5jb20iLCJ1c2VySWQiOjEsImlhdCI6MTcyMzU0Mjc1MCwiZXhwIjoxNzIzNjI5MTUwfQ.placeholder

### 9. Get profile without token (should fail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### 10. Get profile with invalid token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer invalid.token.here

### ===== H2 CONSOLE =====
### Access H2 console (when enabled)
### Open browser: http://localhost:8081/h2-console
### JDBC URL: jdbc:h2:mem:authdb
### Username: sa
### Password: (leave empty)

### ===== USAGE NOTES =====
### 1. Copy the token from login response (step 5)
### 2. Replace the token in step 8 with the actual token
### 3. Or use the @token variable syntax in your HTTP client
### 4. All endpoints validate input according to business rules
### 5. Passwords are hashed with BCrypt for security

